# A guest throws a rock into glass and one into a heavy door: each breaks for everyone, once, by
# the guest's impact claim. The door is the host's and too heavy to take, so the rock's flight ends
# on the contact and its release reaches the host before the claim.
scenario throw_glass_door
scene glass_door
guests 1
settle 8s

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 20ms loss 2%

p1 grab rock_a as lift_a
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw glass speed 7 as glass
p1 wait 1s
p1 walk rock_b
p1 grab rock_b as lift_b
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw door speed 9 as door

expect result lift_a granted
expect result lift_b granted
expect result glass done
expect result door done
expect effect glass
expect effect door
expect effects_once
# Both breaks came by the guest's claims, and an honest guest sends nothing the parser refuses.
expect claims.count >= 2
expect claim_effects.count >= 2
expect claims_format.count <= 0
# The door ends the rock's flight on contact in both modes, so its claim is judged after the
# release (under interaction the glass is judged while the guest still owns the rock).
expect claims_ended.count >= 1
# Derived as in layer_bounce: float noise, 1 cm.
expect local_correction.max <= 1cm
# Derived: the stand takes the thrown body's pose at the throw's first tick; one step at a throw's
# speed (7 m/s and up: 12 cm) carries it past the 5 cm a move needs, and the seam never holds a
# body its thrower simulates: 1.
expect own_ticks.max <= 1t
expect agree_at_rest 5cm 5deg
expect no_stuck
